          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "On Victoria’s Mornington Peninsula, luxury real estate marketing has shifted dramatically from traditional print listings toward **cinematic video storytelling, architectural appreciation, and Instagram-first digital campaigns**. \n\nThe boutique and prestige agencies that have built reputations around this modern, high-impact approach include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **WHITEFOX Real Estate (Peninsula)**\n* **The Reputation:** Widely considered the pioneer of disruptive, entertainment-style property marketing in Victoria. WHITEFOX treats listing campaigns more like high-end fashion and architectural documentaries than traditional property sales.\n* **Video & Social Style:** Fast-paced, punchy, cinematic trailers with stylized color grading, edgy soundtracks, and vertical video formats built natively for Instagram Reels and TikTok. They focus heavily on punchy copywriting (“The Deal”) and lifestyle hype.\n* **Property Focus:** Modern architectural builds, minimalist concrete/timber coastal retreats, high-end new builds, and luxury compounds from Mount Eliza down to Portsea.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Danckert Real Estate (Mount Martha / Mornington)**\n* **The Reputation:** A truly design-literate, boutique agency founded by Sam and Alex Danckert. Unlike agencies that rely on flashy theatrics, Danckert leans into refined editorial branding that mirrors publications like *The Local Project* or *Vogue Living*.\n* **Video & Social Style:** Understated, beautifully paced video tours emphasizing textures, natural light, spatial flow, and craftsmanship. Their social feed is curated like an interior design lookbook rather than a transactional real estate page.\n* **Property Focus:** Mid-century modern revivals, designer beach houses, and contemporary, architect-designed coastal homes across Mount Martha, Mornington, and Mount Eliza.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Kay & Burton (Flinders / Sorrento / Portsea)**\n* **The Reputation:** The gold standard for blue-chip, heritage, and trophy architecture across Melbourne and the southern Peninsula. While an established prestige agency, their contemporary marketing arm operates with boutique precision.\n* **Video & Social Style:** High-budget, documentary-grade films that often interview the architects, landscape designers, or artisans behind the build. Their campaigns feature sweeping aerial cinematography, classical/ambient soundscapes, and targeted digital distribution aimed at Melbourne's metro elite and expat buyers.\n* **Property Focus:** Landmark clifftop architectural compounds, multi-acre Flinders estates, and custom coastal residences crafted by leading Australian architects (e.g., Carr, Rob Mills, Wood Marsh).\n\n---\n\n### 4. **McEwing & Partners (Mount Eliza / Mornington)**\n* **The Reputation:** A premier boutique force anchored in the northern end of the Peninsula (including Mount Eliza’s exclusive Golden Mile and Canadian Bay areas).\n* **Video & Social Style:** Engaging, presenter-led architectural walkthroughs, behind-the-scenes staging reels, and detailed design breakdowns on social media. They excel at conveying family livability while honoring high-spec interior finishes (Venetian plaster, natural stone, seamless indoor-outdoor transitions).\n* **Property Focus:** Turnkey luxury family homes, cliff-edge modernist builds, and bespoke coastal residences.\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Peninsula Sotheby’s International Realty (Sorrento / Flinders / Portsea)**\n* **The Reputation:** Led locally by Rob Curtain, this team handles some of the highest-value transactions on the Mornington Peninsula. \n* **Video & Social Style:** Sweeping, ultra-high-definition video tours highlighting dramatic coastal topography (Bass Strait cliffs, Port Phillip Bay shorelines) paired with modern lifestyle vignettes. They pair social video marketing with global syndicated distribution to reach international and interstate ultra-high-net-worth buyers.\n* **Property Focus:** Landmark coastal architecture, sprawling vineyard estates, and multi-million-dollar waterfront compounds.\n\n---\n\n### Quick Comparison for Sellers & Enthusiasts:\n* **For bold, high-energy, viral social video:** Go to **WHITEFOX**.\n* **For design-focused, artistic, aesthetic curation:** Look at **Danckert Real Estate**.\n* **For museum-grade architectural homes & prestige films:** Look at **Kay & Burton** or **Peninsula Sotheby’s**.",
